{{!-- What a set of improvement results does to the steading, and the controls that do it.

      ONE CONTROL PER RESULT. A line the sheet can write carries its own Apply, and once applied its
      own Revert — every applied line is independently revertable BECAUSE it was independently
      applied. What this replaced was a checkbox per line plus a single Apply, which meant a mis-click
      could not be undone at all and the ticks only meant anything at the moment the button was
      pressed. Most improvements have exactly one writable line; tick-then-commit was ceremony.

      A line the sheet CANNOT write carries no control and says why: a die the table rolls, a
      condition it cannot evaluate, an arithmetic that bends a step it never performs, or pure
      fiction. Giving "draw it on the map" a control that does nothing is what the old checkboxes did.

      A result that confers a MOVE gets something to roll instead: what it does depends on what it
      rolls, so there is nothing to apply in advance.

      TWO COLUMNS, source then result. A row used to be one run-on sentence — "Mill when the autumn
      harvest is complete, the steading generates +1 Surplus" — under a heading that had just said
      when. The heading states the trigger; the row says only WHICH improvement and WHAT IT DOES, in
      their own columns, so the part that differs between rows is the part the eye lands on.

      Except where the caller asks for the line's own `phrase` — the book's trigger clause, on a
      surface with no step, tier or panel around the row to have said it. The clause opens the
      sentence the result finishes, and it is the one place a result's qualifier is stated: "only if
      the market is active" was the fiction the clause already carried, said a second time in the
      sheet's voice. A line that has a clause withholds its timing chip, the whole group with it:
      the em dash that closes the group is drawn by the span, so an empty one left a stray dash in
      front of a clause that had said its own "when".

      WHICH LINES, from the caller. The statement knows every result that fires; which of them THIS
      block lists is the caller's question, because the season's box shows several of them elsewhere —
      against the step they bend, against the roll they wait on, in the upkeep the steading owes — and
      a result stated twice is the undifferentiated wall this was rebuilt to remove. An improvement's
      own card hands over everything, having no steps to collect anything under.

      Params: statement (TurnoverStatement, for the totals its Apply would write); automaticLines /
      advisoryLines / moveSlugs — the lines and granted moves THIS block lists; showSource — false
      where the source is already the surrounding card; showDelta — false where the line's own words
      already state the number; showTiming — true only where the surrounding section does not already
      say WHEN (an improvement's Henceforth half; never the season's own panel, where the timing is
      the panel); showPhrase — true where nothing around the row has stated the trigger, so the
      clause and the result read as the book's own sentence, and false where a step or a result row
      IS the trigger; bulleted — true where the rows read as a list of clauses under a line of prose
      and take the book's swirl, false where they are a table with controls in it and a bullet would be
      marking a form; applyAllAction/applyAllSlug/applyAllLabel — an optional group-level "apply
      everything still owed", for the season turnover where 5-10 lines from different improvements
      fire at once. --}}
<div class="steading-statement">

	{{#if automaticLines.length}}
		<ul class="steading-statement-lines{{#if showSource}} steading-statement-lines--sourced{{/if}}{{#unless bulleted}} stonetop-unmarked{{/unless}}">
			{{#each automaticLines}}
				<li class="steading-statement-line{{#if isApplied}} is-applied{{/if}}">
					{{#if (and ../showTiming timingKeys.length)}}<span class="steading-statement-whens">{{#each timingKeys}}<span class="steading-statement-when">{{localize this}}</span>{{/each}}</span>{{/if}}
					{{#if ../showSource}}<span class="steading-statement-source">{{source}}</span>{{/if}}
					<span class="steading-statement-clause">{{#if (and ../showPhrase phrase)}}{{rich phrase}}, {{/if}}{{rich text}}</span>

					{{#if ../showDelta}}
						{{#with delta}}
							<span class="steading-statement-delta">{{amount}} {{localize subjectKey}}</span>
						{{/with}}
					{{/if}}

					{{#if @root.editable}}
						{{#if isApplied}}
							{{#if canRevert}}
								<button type="button" class="steading-statement-line-btn is-revert"
								        data-action="revertEffectLine" data-line-id="{{id}}"
								        aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.steading.effects.revertLine' result=text.raw}}">
									{{localize "stonetop.steading.effects.revert"}}
								</button>
							{{else}}
								{{!-- Applied before the sheet recorded WHAT each line wrote, so there is no
								      inverse to offer. Stated rather than hidden: it did happen. --}}
								<span class="steading-statement-line-state">{{localize "stonetop.steading.effects.appliedLegacy"}}</span>
							{{/if}}
						{{else}}
							{{!-- Named for the result it applies, not just "Apply": on a card with two of them the
							      bare word says nothing about which line it belongs to, to a reader or to a
							      screen reader. --}}
							<button type="button" class="steading-statement-line-btn"
							        data-action="applyEffectLine" data-line-id="{{id}}"
							        aria-label="{{localize 'stonetop.steading.effects.applyLine' result=text.raw}}">
								{{localize "stonetop.steading.effects.apply"}}
							</button>
						{{/if}}
					{{else if isApplied}}
						<span class="steading-statement-line-state">{{localize "stonetop.steading.effects.applied"}}</span>
					{{/if}}
				</li>
			{{/each}}
		</ul>
	{{/if}}

	{{!-- Advisory lines are shown where the improvement's own words are NOT — the Season tab, where
	      "because of what Stonetop has built" is the whole point. --}}
	{{#if advisoryLines.length}}
		{{!-- No control: nothing here is the sheet's to do. Shown so the table can do it. --}}
		<ul class="steading-statement-lines steading-statement-lines--advisory{{#if showSource}} steading-statement-lines--sourced{{/if}}{{#unless bulleted}} stonetop-unmarked{{/unless}}">
			{{#each advisoryLines}}
					<li class="steading-statement-line">
						{{#if (and ../showTiming timingKeys.length)}}<span class="steading-statement-whens">{{#each timingKeys}}<span class="steading-statement-when">{{localize this}}</span>{{/each}}</span>{{/if}}
						{{#if ../showSource}}<span class="steading-statement-source">{{source}}</span>{{/if}}
						<span class="steading-statement-clause">{{#if (and ../showPhrase phrase)}}{{rich phrase}}, {{/if}}{{rich text}}</span>
						{{#if ../showDelta}}
							{{#with delta}}
								<span class="steading-statement-delta is-advisory">{{amount}} {{localize subjectKey}}</span>
							{{/with}}
						{{/if}}
					</li>
			{{/each}}
		</ul>
	{{/if}}

	{{!-- The moves these results confer, as the moves they are — one row each, with the move's own
	      words behind its disclosure and its own die.

	      What this replaced was a fragment of the move printed as an advisory line AND a "Roll X"
	      button under it: two half-renderings, neither of which was a move, and neither showing the
	      result tiers that ARE the move.

	      The row does NOT name the improvement that conferred it. It used to, since these are
	      collected by when they fire rather than under the thing that granted them — but the caption
	      landed between the move's name and the move's own words, which is the one place on a row
	      nothing else may stand.

	      Not edit-gated: rolling a move writes nothing to the steading, and a locked sheet still gets
	      to roll. --}}
	{{#if moveSlugs.length}}
		<ul class="steading-statement-moves stonetop-unmarked">
			{{#each moveSlugs}}
				{{#with (lookup @root.stonetop.grantedMoves this)}}
					{{> "stonetop.move-row" showCheck=false categoryKey="granted" allowAdditional=false
					    alwaysShowResource=false disclosure=true}}
				{{/with}}
			{{/each}}
		</ul>
	{{/if}}

	{{!-- Batching earns its keep only where several lines from DIFFERENT improvements fire at once,
	      which is the season turnover. There is no batch on an improvement's own card, so no totals
	      either: a before → after is what makes a batch reviewable before you commit to it. --}}
	{{#if (and @root.editable applyAllAction statement.willChangeAnything)}}
		<div class="steading-statement-foot">
			{{#if statement.totals}}
				<span class="steading-statement-totals">
					{{#each statement.totals}}
						<span class="steading-statement-total">
							{{localize (concat "stonetop.steading.attr." target)}}
							<span class="steading-statement-from">{{from}}</span>
							<span class="steading-statement-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
							<span class="steading-statement-to">{{to}}</span>
						</span>
					{{/each}}
				</span>
			{{/if}}

			<button type="button" class="steading-statement-apply" data-action="{{applyAllAction}}"
			        data-slug="{{applyAllSlug}}">
				{{localize applyAllLabel}}
			</button>
		</div>
	{{/if}}

</div>
